.\" man/man3/Docv::Viewer.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Viewer" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer \- A full\-screen terminal viewer for a \fB\%Document\fR: a manual page or a Markdown document.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Viewer\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A full\-screen terminal viewer for a \fB\%Document\fR: a manual page or a
Markdown document. The title row holds the title (a click opens the
help), the page\(aqs heading centered (the manual and the page reference,
or the file name and first heading of a document; the page footer\(aqs
source and date beside it under the pointer) and a close mark; below it
a framed page whose right and bottom borders are draggable scrollbars,
and a status row. The page lays out wrapped or unwrapped and has links with back navigation
(cross\-references, files, heading anchors; URLs go to the terminal as
OSC 8 hyperlinks) and mouse text selection copied to the clipboard.
.PP
A dock (\fB\%Dock\fR) left of the page holds the search field and the tree of
the current page\(aqs group, or of the project\(aqs pages and documents
(\fB\%Index\fR), names sharing a prefix folded into nested groups
(\fB\%Picker::Outline\fR), the current page selected. Text in the field
fuzzy\-finds in the lines of the displayed page, highlighting the matches
in place and scrolling to the best one, while the tree shows how many
lines of its pages match (\fB\%Corpus\fR); text that starts with \fB\%/\fR ranks
every page of the manual instead. The mouse pointer takes the shape of
what it is over (OSC 22).
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
Docv::Viewer.new(Docv.open("ls", "1").not_nil!).run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Without a document the viewer starts on an empty page, the dock closed;
performing \fB\%Action::OpenPage\fR before \fB\%run\fR starts in a search of every
page:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
viewer = Docv::Viewer.new
viewer.perform(Docv::Viewer::Action::OpenPage)
viewer.run
.EE
.RE
