.TP 4
\fBWORD_CHARS = Set {\(aq_\(aq, \(aq\-\(aq}\fR
Characters a double click selects along with letters and digits, so
it takes \fB\%\-\-color\fR and \fB\%snake_case\fR whole.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(document : Document = Document.new, path : String | Nil = nil, wrap : Bool = true, manpath : Manpath = Manpath.default, tty : Term::Tty = Term::Tty.new, options : Options = Options.new, theme : Theme = Theme.new, depth : ColorDepth = Term::Tty.color_depth, settings : ViewerSettings = ViewerSettings.new)\fR
\fIoptions\fR (unsafe requests, syntax highlighting) applies to pages
opened through links and the page search; \fB\%.rd\fR never reads there,
since the terminal belongs to the viewer.
\fItheme\fR styles the viewer (\fB\%Config#theme\fR); its colors follow the
terminal theme once the terminal answers the OSC 21 query, and are
off with \fB\%NO_COLOR\fR (\fIdepth\fR). \fIsettings\fR places the dock and sets
the threads that search the text of all pages (\fB\%Config#viewer\fR).
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef bindings : Bindings\fR
.PP
\fBdef bindings=(bindings : Bindings)\fR
.PP
\fBdef field_bindings : FieldBindings\fR
.PP
\fBdef field_bindings=(field_bindings : FieldBindings)\fR
.PP
\fBdef focus : Focus\fR
.PP
\fBdef page : Page\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef perform(action : Action) : Nil\fR
Runs \fIaction\fR as if its key was pressed in the page view.
.TP 4
\fBdef run : Nil\fR
Runs the viewer until the user quits. Restores the terminal on exit and
saves the page search index.
.PP
\fBdef tree_bindings : TreeBindings\fR
.PP
\fBdef tree_bindings=(tree_bindings : TreeBindings)\fR
.PP
\fBdef wrap? : Bool\fR
